{"base_rate":0.24242424242424243,"brier":0.14037258953168044,"bss":0.2356712500000001,"bss_hi":0.3440176050420167,"bss_lo":0.10433303488349252,"chart":{"base":[376.3,168.2],"fp":[201.4,173.4],"lead":"62,241.4 272,209.8 482,170.1 692,91.1","note":{"base":"skill 0.24 — higher than 25% of cities","fp":"low end +2pp, high end +29pp","lead":"day-1 error 1.2 °C — better than 46% of cities","rel":"promised 0% → rained 2%; promised 98% → rained 71%"},"rel":"62,457.5 124.9,418 401.9,326.9 682.2,158.3"},"country":"RO","deep":false,"depth":["Rain-probability calibration","Calibration curve","Seasonal split"],"ece":0.10819559228650141,"ess":442.9263557818087,"html":{"answer":"\n<h2 id=\"answer\">The short answer for Arad</h2>\n<div class=\"verdict\">\n<p class=\"lead\"><b>The Arad rain forecast is moderately skilful, though 4 points on its probability scale are off by more than chance explains.</b></p>\n<p>When it says rain is <i>near certain</i> (98%), believe about\n<b>71%</b>. When it says rain is <i>very unlikely</i>\n(0%), there is still roughly a <b>2%</b> chance.</p>\n<p class=\"muted\">Based on 726 days, 2024-04-26 to\n2026-05-30. \"Rain\" means at least 0.2 mm measured at\nARAD, 6.1 km from the forecast grid point.\nSkill score 0.24, ranked 100 of\n134 &mdash; but see the rank <i>range</i>\n(59&ndash;119) before reading anything into\nthat position.</p>\n</div>\n\n<h3>What the percentages actually mean here</h3>\n<div class=\"tablewrap\">\n<table><thead><tr><th class=\"num\">It said</th><th class=\"num\">It rained</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Days</th><th>Verdict</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td class='num'>0%</td><td class='num'><b>2%</b></td><td class='num'>254</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">underpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>4%</td><td class='num'><b>6%</b></td><td class='num'>94</td><td><span class=\"tag good\">honest</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>16%</td><td class='num'><b>16%</b></td><td class='num'>86</td><td><span class=\"tag good\">honest</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>38%</td><td class='num'><b>24%</b></td><td class='num'>72</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>69%</td><td class='num'><b>41%</b></td><td class='num'>74</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>98%</td><td class='num'><b>71%</b></td><td class='num'>146</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr></tbody></table>\n</div>\n<p class=\"muted\">4 of 6 groups are further from honest than chance\nalone can explain. The rest are indistinguishable from a perfect forecast.</p>\n","card":"\n<div class=\"gcard\">\n  <p class=\"gcard-head\"><b>Arad</b> <span class=\"muted\">RO</span></p>\n  <p class=\"gcard-tier\"><span class=\"tag ok\">Moderately skilful</span>\n    <span class=\"muted\">4 points off by more than chance</span></p>\n  <dl class=\"gcard-stats\">\n    <div><dt>Skill score</dt><dd>0.24</dd></div>\n    <div><dt>Rank</dt><dd>59&ndash;119\n      <span class=\"muted\">of 134</span></dd></div>\n    <div><dt>Record</dt><dd>726 <span class=\"muted\">days</span></dd></div>\n  </dl>\n  <p class=\"gcard-more\"><a href=\"#answer\">The full verdict for\n    Arad &darr;</a></p>\n</div>","curve":"\n<h2 id=\"curve\">The calibration curve</h2>\n<p>Each dot is a group of days sharing a similar forecast. Horizontal position\nis what was promised; vertical is what happened. <b>On the dashed diagonal =\nhonest.</b> Hover any dot for its sample size.</p>\n<figure><svg viewBox=\"0 0 430 430\" width=\"100%\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Calibration curve for Arad\"><rect class=\"chart-plot\" x=\"58\" y=\"18\" width=\"354\" height=\"364\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"58\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"382\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"58\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">0%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"386\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">0%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"146.5\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"146.5\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"291.0\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"291.0\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"146.5\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">25%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"295.0\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">25%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"235.0\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"235.0\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"200.0\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"200.0\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"235.0\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">50%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"204.0\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">50%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"323.5\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"323.5\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"109.0\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"109.0\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"323.5\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">75%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"113.0\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">75%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"412\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"18\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"18\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"412\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">100%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"22\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">100%</text><polygon class=\"chart-band\" points=\"58.01393700787401,382.0 73.06382978723404,351.02127659574467 115.46325581395348,293.1162790697674 192.76583333333335,205.05555555555557 303.742972972973,91.7837837837838 406.52027397260275,18.0 406.52027397260275,30.46575342465752 303.742972972973,165.56756756756755 192.76583333333335,280.8888888888889 115.46325581395348,348.13953488372096 73.06382978723404,378.1276595744681 58.01393700787401,382.0\" opacity=\"0.16\"/><line class=\"chart-ideal\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"18\" stroke-dasharray=\"5,4\" stroke-width=\"1.3\"/><line class=\"chart-base\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"293.75757575757575\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"293.75757575757575\" stroke-dasharray=\"2,3\"/><polyline class=\"chart-line\" points=\"58.01393700787401,374.8346456692913 73.06382978723404,358.7659574468085 115.46325581395348,322.74418604651163 192.76583333333335,296.05555555555554 303.742972972973,234.43243243243242 406.52027397260275,122.71232876712332\" fill=\"none\" stroke-width=\"2.4\"/><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 0%&amp;#10;It rained 2% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 254 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"58.01393700787401\" cy=\"374.8346456692913\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 4%&amp;#10;It rained 6% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 94 days&amp;#10;within the range a perfect forecast would give\"><circle class=\"chart-dot\" cx=\"73.06382978723404\" cy=\"358.7659574468085\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 16%&amp;#10;It rained 16% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 86 days&amp;#10;within the range a perfect forecast would give\"><circle class=\"chart-dot\" cx=\"115.46325581395348\" cy=\"322.74418604651163\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 38%&amp;#10;It rained 24% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 72 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"192.76583333333335\" cy=\"296.05555555555554\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 69%&amp;#10;It rained 41% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 74 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"303.742972972973\" cy=\"234.43243243243242\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 98%&amp;#10;It rained 71% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 146 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"406.52027397260275\" cy=\"122.71232876712332\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><text class=\"chart-label\" x=\"235.0\" y=\"422\" font-size=\"12.5\" text-anchor=\"middle\">What the forecast promised</text><text class=\"chart-label\" x=\"15\" y=\"200.0\" font-size=\"12.5\" text-anchor=\"middle\" transform=\"rotate(-90 15 200.0)\">How often it actually rained</text></svg>\n<figcaption>Green band = where a <b>flawless</b> forecast would still land, given\nhow few days we have. Red dots fall outside it, so those are real errors rather\nthan noise. The faint horizontal line is climatology\n(24%).</figcaption></figure>\n","season":"\n<h2 id=\"season\">Does the season matter?</h2>\n<p>In Arad the forecast is most skilful in\n<b>spring</b> (0.41) and least in\n<b>winter</b> (-0.00).</p>\n<div class=\"tablewrap\">\n<table><thead><tr><th>Season</th><th class=\"num\">Days</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Rain days</th><th class=\"num\">Skill score</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Avg error</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>winter</td><td class='num'>175</td><td class='num'>30%</td><td class='num'>-0.005</td><td class='num'>17.1%</td></tr><tr><td>summer</td><td class='num'>155</td><td class='num'>15%</td><td class='num'>0.115</td><td class='num'>11.2%</td></tr><tr><td>autumn</td><td class='num'>180</td><td class='num'>24%</td><td class='num'>0.317</td><td class='num'>9.1%</td></tr><tr><td>spring</td><td class='num'>216</td><td class='num'>26%</td><td class='num'>0.409</td><td class='num'>10.0%</td></tr></tbody></table>\n</div>\n<p class=\"muted\">Four-way splits of a two-year record are thin, so read the\nordering as indicative. Coarser binning is used here than for the annual curve\nfor the same reason.</p>\n"},"lat":46.18333,"lon":21.31667,"n":726,"n_cities":134,"name":"Arad","offset_days":-1,"pop_map":[{"hi":0.02,"lo":0.0,"mean":3.937007874015748e-05,"n":254,"obs":0.01968503937007874,"sig":true},{"hi":0.1,"lo":0.02,"mean":0.0425531914893617,"n":94,"obs":0.06382978723404255,"sig":false},{"hi":0.27,"lo":0.1,"mea